From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: The video memory budget follows dxgi.maxDeviceMemory
 and dxgi.maxSharedMemory

QueryVideoMemoryInfo reported each heap's whole budget whatever the
adapter's description was capped to, and engines size their texture
pools from the budget. On a device whose video memory is shared with
the CPU's (a console), a game that took the whole 8 GB heap as its
own ran the system out of memory: the budget and the memory that can
be reserved now keep to the same cap.
---
 src/dxgi/dxgi_adapter.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/dxgi/dxgi_adapter.cpp b/src/dxgi/dxgi_adapter.cpp
index 27152e6..31774bd 100644
--- a/src/dxgi/dxgi_adapter.cpp
+++ b/src/dxgi/dxgi_adapter.cpp
@@ -287,6 +287,19 @@ namespace dxvk {
       pVideoMemoryInfo->AvailableForReservation += memInfo.heaps[i].heapSize / 2;
     }
 
+    // The memory reported to the game is capped (dxgi.maxDeviceMemory, dxgi.maxSharedMemory):
+    // the budget too, which engines size their texture pools from, not only the adapter's
+    // description. On a device whose video memory is shared with the CPU's, a game that
+    // sized itself from the whole heap ran the system out of memory.
+    const DxgiOptions* options = m_factory->GetOptions();
+    VkDeviceSize limit = MemorySegmentGroup == DXGI_MEMORY_SEGMENT_GROUP_LOCAL
+      ? options->maxDeviceMemory : options->maxSharedMemory;
+
+    if (limit > 0) {
+      pVideoMemoryInfo->Budget = std::min<UINT64>(pVideoMemoryInfo->Budget, limit);
+      pVideoMemoryInfo->AvailableForReservation = std::min<UINT64>(pVideoMemoryInfo->AvailableForReservation, limit / 2);
+    }
+
     // We don't implement reservation, but the observable
     // behaviour should match that of Windows drivers
     uint32_t segmentId = uint32_t(MemorySegmentGroup);
